        "original_id": "5a560d7b-1e0a-595d-9765-5cc251a50ce7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hugh Keays-Byrne, George Miller, Byron Kennedy, Mel Gibson, Joanne Samuel, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, Roger Ward, Igor Auzins, Miles Buchanan, Simone Buchanan, Kate Fitzpatrick, Ron Haddrick\n- Works: Stone, Mad Max, Farscape, Runaway Island\n- Roles: Toad, Toecutter, Immortan Joe, Grunchlk, Mad Max Rockatansky\n\nFacts:\n- In 1974, Hugh Keays-Byrne played Toad in the film Stone.\n- In 1979, Mad Max was released as an Australian dystopian action film directed by George Miller and produced by Byron Kennedy.\n- In 1979, Mad Max starred Mel Gibson as Mad Max Rockatansky alongside Joanne Samuel, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, and Roger Ward.\n- In 1979, Hugh Keays-Byrne played the main antagonist Toecutter in Mad Max.\n- In 1982, Runaway Island was released as an Australian television film directed by Igor Auzins.\n- In 1982, Runaway Island starred Miles Buchanan, Simone Buchanan, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Kate Fitzpatrick, and Ron Haddrick.\n- Hugh Keays-Byrne later played Grunchlk in the science fiction television series Farscape.\n- Hugh Keays-Byrne later played the main antagonist Immortan Joe in the 2015 film named in the source sentence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
